lines[10]:
  - i, text, start, end
  - 0, What happens if you hold your breath for as long as you can?, 0.35, 3.524
  - 1, "For the first thirty seconds, nothing much.", 3.784, 6.048
  - 2, "Your lungs are full, and your blood is still carrying plenty of oxygen.", 6.308, 10.764
  - 3, "But carbon dioxide starts building up,", 11.024, 13.394
  - 4, "and that, not the lack of oxygen, is what makes you desperate to breathe.", 13.914, 18.332
  - 5, "Your diaphragm starts twitching, trying to force a breath,", 18.592, 21.872
  - 6, and your heart actually slows down to save oxygen., 22.352, 25.568
  - 7, "Push even further, and your brain simply switches you off.", 25.828, 29.208
  - 8, "You pass out, and your body starts breathing again on its own.", 29.468, 32.976
  - 9, Which is why you should never try this underwater., 33.236, 36.183
